				<r3d:description language="eng">DataStream is an open access platform for sharing information on freshwater health. It currently allows users to access, visualize, and download full water quality datasets collected by Indigenous Nations, community groups, researchers and governments throughout five regional hubs: Atlantic Canada, the Great Lakes and Saint Lawrence region, the Lake Winnipeg Basin, the Mackenzie River Basin and the Pacific region. DataStream was developed by The Gordon Foundation and is carried out in collaboration with regional monitoring networks.</r3d:description>
